# Flutter Widget Structure

Formatting and lints cannot flatten widget trees; structure must do it.

- Keep each `build` method shallow: about 6 levels of widget nesting at most.
  When deeper, extract a widget.
- Extract widget classes, not `Widget _buildX()` helper methods.
- Split screens into roles:
  - App shell (`MaterialApp`, theme, routing) only.
  - Screen: page content as a flat `children` list.
  - Layout wrapper: `Scaffold`, `SafeArea`, `Center`, scroll, width constraint.
  - Small leaf widgets for styled pieces (boxes, cards, rows).
- Never use `Builder` just to get a context below `MaterialApp`/`Scaffold`;
  extract a widget so its own `build` context is in the right place.
- Make extracted widgets private (`_Name`) unless another file needs them.
  Reuse shared layouts (e.g. `AuthScaffold`) before writing a new one.
- Read `Theme.of(context)` inside the widget that uses it, not by passing
  `ThemeData` down.
- Keep extracted widgets `const`-constructible where possible.

```dart
// BAD: content buried under shell and layout
home: Builder(builder: (context) => Scaffold(body: SafeArea(child: Center(
  child: SingleChildScrollView(child: ConstrainedBox(child: Column(...)))))))

// GOOD: each layer is its own widget
home: _SetupScreen(details: details),

class _SetupScreen extends StatelessWidget {
  Widget build(BuildContext context) =>
      _CenteredScrollLayout(children: [/* flat content */]);
}
```

After edits, run `dart format` and `flutter analyze` on changed files.
